   "type": "text",
   "text": "# Security Review: `interface/forms/eye_mag/report.php`\n\n## Summary\n\nThis file should not be merged as written. It has:\n- an unauthenticated-by-ACL patient-context override (IDOR),\n- a request-driven SQL injection,\n- widespread stored and reflected XSS of PHI fields,\n- several insecure-design issues: variable-variable injection, `extract()`, and publicly served signature images.\n\n| # | Location | OWASP 2021 | Severity |\n|---|----------|------------|----------|\n| 1 | Top-level `$_REQUEST['ptid' / 'encid' / 'formid' / 'formname']` | A01 Broken Access Control | **High** |\n| 2 | `display_draw_image()` \u2013 `documents.url like '%\".$filename.\"'` | A03 Injection (SQLi) + A01 | **High / Critical** |\n| 3 | Multiple raw `echo`s of clinical fields | A03 Injection (Stored XSS) | **High** |\n| 4 | `$pid` in `<img src>` (photo and drawing sections) | A03 Injection (Reflected XSS) | **High** |\n| 5 | `narrative()` \u2013 `\"select * from facility where id=\" . $_SESSION['pc_facility']` | A03 Injection (SQLi) | Medium |\n| 6 | `$$LOCATION = text($prefs['GOVALUE'])` | A04 Insecure Design / A08 | Medium |\n| 7 | `@extract($objQuery)` / `@extract($encounter_data)` | A04 Insecure Design | Low\u2013Medium |\n| 8 | Provider signatures at `/interface/forms/eye_mag/images/sign_<id>.jpg` | A05 Misconfiguration / A01 | Medium |\n| 9 | \"electronically signed on <today>\" applied unconditionally | A08 Data Integrity | Medium |\n| 10 | Encounter/form queries with missing constraints | A01 Broken Access Control | Low |\n| 11 | No PHI-access audit for cross-patient views | A09 Logging & Monitoring | Low |\n\n---\n\n## 1. Patient/encounter context overridable from the request (IDOR)\n\n**Category:** A01 Broken Access Control. **Severity: High.**\n\n```php\nif ($_REQUEST['ptid']) $pid = $_REQUEST['ptid'];\nif ($_REQUEST['encid']) $encounter=$_REQUEST['encid'];\nif ($_REQUEST['formid']) $form_id = $_REQUEST['formid'];\nif ($_REQUEST['formname']) $form_name=$_REQUEST['formname'];\n```\n\n**The problem:**\n- This runs at global scope whenever the file is included, and it overwrites the session-bound `$pid` and `$encounter`.\n- Report callers (encounter summary, `encounters_ajax.php`, custom reports, fax/taskman) include `*_report.php` and then call `eye_mag_report($pid, $encounter, \u2026)` using these globals.\n- Any authenticated user can therefore add `?ptid=X&encid=Y` and render another patient's full exam: HPI, PMSFH, photo, drawings, Rx and plan.\n- Any code in the including page that runs after the include also operates on the attacker-chosen patient.\n- `acl.inc` is included, but `acl_check()` is never called. There is no check that the user may access this patient's encounters or this form type.\n\n**Fix:**\n- Remove the overrides, or restrict them to a trusted internal caller.\n- Cast the values to integers.\n- Enforce `acl_check('patients','med')` (and encounter/sensitivity checks) before rendering.\n\n## 2. SQL injection in `display_draw_image()`\n\n**Category:** A03 Injection, with A01 consequences. **Severity: High/Critical.**\n\n```php\n$base_name = $pid.\"_\".$encounter.\"_\".$side.\"_\".$zone.\"_VIEW\";\n$filename = $base_name.\".jpg\";\n$sql = \"SELECT * from documents where documents.url like '%\".$filename.\"'\";\n$doc = sqlQuery($sql);\n```\n\n**SQL injection:**\n- `$pid` and `$encounter` come directly from `$_REQUEST['ptid']` and `$_REQUEST['encid']` (issue 1).\n- `$sanitize_all_escapes=true` disables OpenEMR's legacy auto-escaping, so the values reach the query unescaped.\n- A payload such as `ptid=1' UNION SELECT ... -- ` allows arbitrary data extraction from the database, including the `users` table and password hashes.\n\n**Even without injection, the LIKE pattern leaks other patients' documents:**\n- The leading `%` means `pid=1, encounter=5` matches `\u2026/11_5_OU_EXT_VIEW.jpg`, `21_5_\u2026`, and so on.\n- `_` is an unescaped LIKE wildcard.\n- As a result, another patient's drawing (and its notes, which are output raw, see issue 3) can be displayed.\n\n**Fix:**\n- Use a bound parameter.\n- Match on exact `foreign_id = ?` plus the exact URL suffix, with `_` and `%` escaped.\n\n## 3. Stored XSS: PHI fields echoed without encoding\n\n**Category:** A03 Injection (XSS). **Severity: High.**\n\nMost fields correctly use `text()`, but the following are output raw:\n\n| Location | Raw output |\n|---|---|\n| HPI line | `echo $HPI1;` (`HPI2`/`HPI3` are escaped, `HPI1` is not) |\n| Chronic problems | `echo \"&nbsp;\".$CHRONIC2`, `echo \"&nbsp;\".$CHRONIC3` |\n| Impression/Plan | `echo $item['codetext']`, `echo $item['code']` (with `codetype`), `echo $item['plan']` (only newline\u2192`<br />` replacement) |\n| Orders | `echo $item.\"<br />\"` for each `explode('|',$PLAN)`, and `echo $PLAN2` |\n| Contact lens | `echo ($CTLOSVA?:\"-\")` |\n| Motility grid | `$$zone[$i] = \"-\".$$zone[$i]` then `echo $MOTILITY_*`. The check `>= '1'` passes for strings like `\"1<script>\u2026\"`. |\n| Drawing notes | `echo '<td>'.$note->get_note().'\u2026'` |\n| PDF signature block | `$providerNAME` (escaped a few lines later, but not here) |\n| Additional data table | `$display_Add` in a class attribute (uninitialized and unescaped) |\n| Image paths | `$form_folder` in image paths (constant today, but should be `attr()`) |\n\n**Impact:**\n- Any user who can edit an eye exam, problem list, or document note can plant script.\n- That script runs in the session of every clinician or administrator who views the report or the encounter-history mouse-over, enabling session riding and PHI exfiltration.\n- In PDF mode, injected HTML can also manipulate html2pdf, for example `<img src=\"/etc/...\">` local file references.\n\n**Fix:**\n- Wrap every value in `text()`, or `attr()` for attributes.\n- For multi-line fields use `nl2br(text($x))`.\n\n## 4. Reflected XSS via `ptid`\n\n**Category:** A03 Injection. **Severity: High.**\n\n```php\n$filetoshow = $GLOBALS['webroot'].\"/controller.php?document&retrieve&patient_id=$pid&document_id=...\";\necho \"<img src='\".$filetoshow.\"' style='width:220px;'>\";\n```\n\n**The problem:**\n- In the patient photo block, the lookup is `documents.foreign_id=?` with `$pid = \"1' onerror='alert(document.cookie)\"`.\n- MySQL's string-to-integer coercion matches patient 1, so a photo is found.\n- The unencoded `$pid` then breaks out of the single-quoted `src` attribute.\n- The same pattern occurs in `display_draw_image()`, where the row can be forced via issue 2.\n- `$from_file` is likewise unencoded in PDF mode.\n\n**Fix:**\n- Cast `$pid` and `$encounter` with `(int)`.\n- Build URLs with `attr()` and `urlencode()`.\n\n## 5. Concatenated SQL with session value\n\n**Category:** A03 Injection. **Severity: Medium.**\n\n```php\n$sql = \"select * from facility where id=\" . $_SESSION['pc_facility'];\n```\n\n**The problem:**\n- `pc_facility` is populated from request data in the calendar module in several OpenEMR versions, so it is not a trustworthy integer.\n- This is pre-existing code the change relies on.\n\n**Fix:** use `sqlQuery(\"select * from facility where id=?\", array($_SESSION['pc_facility']))`.\n\n## 6. Variable-variable assignment from DB preferences\n\n**Category:** A04 Insecure Design / A08 Data Integrity. **Severity: Medium.**\n\n```php\n$LOCATION = $prefs['LOCATION'];\n$$LOCATION = text($prefs['GOVALUE']);\n```\n\n**The problem:**\n- This executes at global scope, so any global variable named by a `form_eye_mag_prefs.LOCATION` row is overwritten.\n- That includes `$pid`, `$encounter`, `$form_id`, `$PDF_OUTPUT`, `$GLOBALS` entries, and at global scope even superglobals such as `$_SESSION`.\n- Preferences are user-writable through the eye_mag save endpoint, so a user can tamper with variables in their own request context. That can redirect `$pid` or influence the including page's logic.\n\n**Fix:** store preferences in an array (`$prefs[$LOCATION] = \u2026`) and whitelist the allowed keys.\n\n## 7. `@extract()` of database rows\n\n**Category:** A04 Insecure Design. **Severity: Low\u2013Medium.**\n\n**The problem:**\n- `extract($encounter_data)` pulls in `form_encounter.*` and `form_eye_mag.*`, including columns such as `pid`, `encounter`, `id` and `provider_id`.\n- Local variables used later for authorization-relevant queries (`$pid`, `$encounter`) are silently replaced with whatever column names exist.\n- The `@` suppresses errors, so this happens without any warning.\n- `left_overs()` does the same with `$$key=$value` on undefined `$table_name`/`$id`. It is dead code and should be removed.\n\n**Fix:** access the row as an array, or call `extract()` with `EXTR_SKIP` and a prefix.\n\n## 8. Provider e-signatures served from the web root\n\n**Category:** A05 Security Misconfiguration / A01. **Severity: Medium.**\n\n`images/sign_<providerID>.jpg` lives under `/interface/forms/eye_mag/images/` and is referenced directly by URL.\n\n**The problem:**\n- The provider IDs are sequential integers.\n- Static files are served without OpenEMR authentication, so anyone can enumerate and download every provider's handwritten signature.\n\n**Fix:** store signatures in the documents repository, outside the web root, and serve them through an authenticated controller.\n\n## 9. Misleading electronic signature attestation\n\n**Category:** A08 Software and Data Integrity Failures. **Severity: Medium.**\n\n**The problem:**\n- In PDF/fax mode, the signature image is printed with \"electronically signed on `oeFormatShortDate()`\", which is today's date.\n- This happens whenever the image file exists, regardless of whether the encounter or form was actually signed or locked, or by whom.\n- Faxed and exported documents can therefore falsely appear signed by the provider.\n\n**Fix:** only render the attestation when an actual signature record exists (e.g. `esign_signatures`), using its signer and timestamp.\n\n## 10. Weak query constraints\n\n**Category:** A01 Broken Access Control. **Severity: Low.**\n\n**`eye_mag_report()`:**\n- It does not filter `forms.deleted`.\n- It does not filter `forms.formdir='eye_mag'`.\n\n**`narrative()`:**\n- It joins `form_eye_mag.id=forms.form_id` without `formdir`.\n- It does not tie `forms.pid` to the patient.\n- Rows from deleted forms, or from an unrelated form whose numeric id collides, can therefore be shown.\n\n**Impplan query:**\n- It filters on the caller-supplied `$form_id` and `$pid` only.\n- Combined with issue 1, this lets a user choose arbitrary form/patient pairs.\n\n## 11. Logging and monitoring\n\n**Category:** A09. **Severity: Low.**\n\n**The problem:**\n- Viewing a different patient via `ptid` bypasses the normal \"set active patient\" flow.\n- No explicit audit event (e.g. `newEvent('view', \u2026)`) is written for the patient actually displayed.\n- This makes cross-patient snooping harder to detect in the access log.\n\n---\n\n## Recommended Remediation Order\n\n1. Remove the `$_REQUEST` overrides, or cast them to `(int)` and add `acl_check` plus patient-access checks.\n2. Parameterize and tighten the `documents` lookup in `display_draw_image()`, and parameterize the facility query.\n3. Escape every output with `text()` or `attr()`, especially `HPI1`, `CHRONIC2/3`, IMPPLAN `code`/`codetext`/`plan`, `PLAN`/`PLAN2`, notes, motility values, `$pid` in URLs, and `CTLOSVA`.\n4. Replace `$$LOCATION` and `extract()` with array access.\n5. Move signature images out of the web root and tie the \"electronically signed\" text to real e-sign records.\n6. Add an explicit PHI-view audit entry and remove dead code (`left_overs`, `full_report`)."
  }
